  "grammarNotes": [
    {
      "id": "essen-ein-eine",
      "title": "ein and eine: a / an",
      "body": "**ein** goes before *der* and *das* words, **eine** before *die* words. There is no *a* in the plural: *Äpfel* = apples.",
      "table": [
        ["", "der word", "die word", "das word"],
        ["the", "der Kaffee", "die Milch", "das Wasser"],
        ["a", "ein Kaffee", "eine Milch", "ein Wasser"]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "essen-accusative",
      "title": "The accusative: einen",
      "body": "When a noun is the **object** of a verb (the thing you want, have, eat or drink), it's in the **accusative** case.\n\nOnly **der** words change: *ein* becomes **einen**. *die* and *das* words stay the same.\n\n- *Das ist **ein** Kaffee.* (subject)\n- *Ich möchte **einen** Kaffee.* (object)\n\n*mein, dein, sein* and *ihr* change the same way: *Das ist mein Tee.* → *Ich trinke **meinen** Tee.*",
      "table": [
        ["", "der word", "die word", "das word"],
        ["subject", "ein Tee", "eine Tasse", "ein Bier"],
        ["object", "einen Tee", "eine Tasse", "ein Bier"]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "essen-moechten-haben",
      "title": "möchten and haben",
      "body": "**möchten** (would like) has no *-t* in the *er/sie* form: *sie möchte*. **haben** (to have) drops the *b* in *du hast* and *er hat*.\n\nWith *möchten*, a second verb goes to the **end** of the sentence: *Ich möchte einen Kaffee **trinken**.*",
      "table": [
        ["Person", "möchten", "haben"],
        ["ich", "möchte", "habe"],
        ["du", "möchtest", "hast"],
        ["er / sie / es", "möchte", "hat"],
        ["wir", "möchten", "haben"],
        ["ihr", "möchtet", "habt"],
        ["sie / Sie", "möchten", "haben"]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "essen-essen",
      "title": "essen: e changes to i",
      "body": "Like *sprechen*, **essen** changes *e* to *i* in the *du* and *er/sie/es* forms. In *du isst*, the *s* of the ending merges into the *ss*.",
      "table": [
        ["Person", "essen", "trinken (regular)"],
        ["ich", "esse", "trinke"],
        ["du", "isst", "trinkst"],
        ["er / sie / es", "isst", "trinkt"],
        ["wir", "essen", "trinken"],
        ["ihr", "esst", "trinkt"],
        ["sie / Sie", "essen", "trinken"]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "essen-hunger",
      "title": "Hungry and thirsty",
      "body": "German says *I have hunger*, not *I am hungry*:\n\n- **Ich habe Hunger.** I'm hungry.\n- **Ich habe Durst.** I'm thirsty.\n\nNo article is needed here."
    }
  ],
  "lessons": [
