        {
          "id": "fd2-e7",
          "type": "TEACH",
          "title": "trinken, Glas and Tasse",
          "body": "- **trinken** = to drink (regular)\n- **das Glas** = the glass, **die Tasse** = the cup\n\nWith *möchten*, a second verb goes to the **end** of the sentence: *Was möchtest du **trinken**?*\n\nGerman doesn't need *of*: **ein Glas Wasser** = a glass of water.",
          "examples": [
